# Usafiri Frontend - Development Guidelines

## Project Overview
Multi-tenant shuttle transport booking platform frontend built with React, TypeScript, Redux Toolkit, and Shadcn/ui.

## Design System & UI Standards

### Typography & Spacing
- **Font Size**: Use `text-xs` for most text content
- **Font Color**: Use `text-gray-600` for body text, `text-gray-900` for headings
- **Border & Lines**: Use `border-gray-200` for all borders and dividers
- **Design**: Compact, information-dense layouts

### Component Preferences
- **Lists**: Always use `<Table>` component from Shadcn/ui, never cards or grids
- **Forms & Details**: Use `<Dialog>` modals, avoid full-page forms
- **Buttons**: Small size (`size="sm"`), minimal spacing
- **Layout**: Avoid crowding pages with too many features - one feature per page/section

### Color Palette
```tsx
// Primary text: text-gray-900
// Secondary text: text-gray-600
// Borders: border-gray-200
// Backgrounds: bg-white, bg-gray-50
// Interactive: Use theme colors (primary, destructive, etc.)
```

## Module Structure
Follow the auth module pattern exactly:

```
src/modules/[feature]/
├── __tests__/
│   ├── [feature].api.test.ts
│   ├── [feature]Slice.test.ts
│   └── [Component].test.tsx
├── interfaces/
│   ├── [feature].interface.ts
│   └── index.ts
├── reducers/
│   └── [feature]Slice.ts
├── hooks/
│   └── use[Feature].ts
├── components/
│   └── [Feature]Modal.tsx
├── pages/
│   └── [Feature]List.tsx
└── [feature].api.ts
```

## Redux Patterns

### Slice Structure
```typescript
import { createSlice, createAsyncThunk } from '@reduxjs/toolkit';

interface FeatureState {
  items: Item[];
  selectedItem: Item | null;
  loading: boolean;
  error: string | null;
}

const initialState: FeatureState = {
  items: [],
  selectedItem: null,
  loading: false,
  error: null,
};

// Async thunks
export const fetchItems = createAsyncThunk(
  'feature/fetchItems',
  async () => await api.getAll()
);

const featureSlice = createSlice({
  name: 'feature',
  initialState,
  reducers: {
    setSelectedItem: (state, action) => {
      state.selectedItem = action.payload;
    },
    clearError: (state) => {
      state.error = null;
    },
  },
  extraReducers: (builder) => {
    builder
      .addCase(fetchItems.pending, (state) => {
        state.loading = true;
        state.error = null;
      })
      .addCase(fetchItems.fulfilled, (state, action) => {
        state.loading = false;
        state.items = action.payload;
      })
      .addCase(fetchItems.rejected, (state, action) => {
        state.loading = false;
        state.error = action.error.message || 'Failed to fetch';
      });
  },
});

export const { setSelectedItem, clearError } = featureSlice.actions;
export default featureSlice.reducer;
```

### Register in Store
```typescript
// src/store/index.ts
import featureReducer from '../modules/feature/reducers/featureSlice';

export const store = configureStore({
  reducer: {
    auth: authReducer,
    feature: featureReducer, // Add new reducers here
  },
});
```

## API Integration

### API Client Pattern
```typescript
import { BaseApi } from "../../api/base.api";

class FeatureApi extends BaseApi {
  constructor() {
    super("/endpoint");
  }

  async getAll(): Promise<Item[]> {
    return this.get<Item[]>("");
  }

  async getById(id: string): Promise<Item> {
    return this.get<Item>(`/${id}`);
  }

  async create(data: CreateDto): Promise<Item> {
    return this.post<Item, CreateDto>("", data);
  }

  async update(id: string, data: UpdateDto): Promise<Item> {
    return this.put<Item, UpdateDto>(`/${id}`, data);
  }

  async delete(id: string): Promise<void> {
    return this.delete<void>(`/${id}`);
  }
}

export const featureApi = new FeatureApi();
```

## Custom Hooks Pattern

```typescript
import { useEffect } from 'react';
import { useAppDispatch, useAppSelector } from '../../../store';

export const useFeature = () => {
  const dispatch = useAppDispatch();
  const { items, loading, error } = useAppSelector((state) => state.feature);

  useEffect(() => {
    dispatch(fetchItems());
  }, []);

  const refetch = () => {
    dispatch(fetchItems());
  };

  return { items, loading, error, refetch };
};
```

## Component Patterns

### Table-Based List Page
```tsx
import { useFeature } from "../hooks/useFeature";
import {
  Table,
  TableBody,
  TableCell,
  TableHead,
  TableHeader,
  TableRow,
} from "@/components/ui/table";
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";
import { Skeleton } from "@/components/ui/skeleton";
import { Alert, AlertDescription } from "@/components/ui/alert";

export default function FeatureList() {
  const { items, loading, error } = useFeature();

  if (loading) {
    return (
      <div className="p-4 space-y-2">
        {[1, 2, 3].map((i) => <Skeleton key={i} className="h-8" />)}
      </div>
    );
  }

  if (error) {
    return (
      <div className="p-4">
        <Alert variant="destructive">
          <AlertDescription className="text-xs">{error}</AlertDescription>
        </Alert>
      </div>
    );
  }

  return (
    <div className="p-4">
      <div className="flex justify-between items-center mb-4">
        <h1 className="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">Feature List</h1>
        <Button size="sm">Add New</Button>
      </div>
      
      <div className="border border-gray-200 rounded-md">
        <Table>
          <TableHeader>
            <TableRow className="bg-gray-50">
              <TableHead className="text-xs text-gray-600">Column 1</TableHead>
              <TableHead className="text-xs text-gray-600">Column 2</TableHead>
              <TableHead className="text-xs text-gray-600 text-right">Actions</TableHead>
            </TableRow>
          </TableHeader>
          <TableBody>
            {items.map((item) => (
              <TableRow key={item.id} className="border-gray-200">
                <TableCell className="text-xs text-gray-600">{item.name}</TableCell>
                <TableCell className="text-xs text-gray-600">{item.value}</TableCell>
                <TableCell className="text-right">
                  <Button variant="ghost" size="sm">View</Button>
                </TableCell>
              </TableRow>
            ))}
          </TableBody>
        </Table>
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}
```

### Modal Dialog Pattern
```tsx
import {
  Dialog,
  DialogContent,
  DialogHeader,
  DialogTitle,
  DialogDescription,
} from "@/components/ui/dialog";

interface FeatureModalProps {
  open: boolean;
  onOpenChange: (open: boolean) => void;
  item: Item | null;
}

export function FeatureModal({ open, onOpenChange, item }: FeatureModalProps) {
  return (
    <Dialog open={open} onOpenChange={onOpenChange}>
      <DialogContent className="max-w-2xl">
        <DialogHeader>
          <DialogTitle className="text-lg text-gray-900">Feature Details</DialogTitle>
          <DialogDescription className="text-xs text-gray-600">
            View and edit feature information
          </DialogDescription>
        </DialogHeader>
        
        <div className="space-y-3">
          {/* Content with text-xs and text-gray-600 */}
        </div>
      </DialogContent>
    </Dialog>
  );
}
```

## Testing Requirements

### All modules MUST have tests for:
1. API client methods
2. Redux slice (actions, reducers, thunks)
3. Custom hooks
4. Page components
5. Modal components

### Test File Pattern
```typescript
import { describe, it, expect, vi, beforeEach } from 'vitest';
import { renderHook, waitFor } from '@testing-library/react';
import { Provider } from 'react-redux';
import { configureStore } from '@reduxjs/toolkit';

describe('Feature Module', () => {
  describe('API', () => {
    it('should fetch items', async () => {
      // Test implementation
    });
  });

  describe('Redux Slice', () => {
    it('should handle fetchItems.fulfilled', () => {
      // Test implementation
    });
  });

  describe('useFeature Hook', () => {
    it('should fetch items on mount', async () => {
      // Test implementation
    });
  });
});
```

## Navigation & Routing

### Adding New Features

**1. Add route in `src/routes/index.tsx`:**
```typescript
import FeatureList from "../modules/feature/pages/FeatureList";

export const adminRoutes: RoutesProps[] = [
  {
    path: "/features",
    name: "Features",
    breadcrumb: [{ label: "Features", path: "/features" }],
    element: <FeatureList />,
    roles: [], // or specific roles
    requiresAuth: true,
  },
];
```

**2. Add sidebar link in `src/modules/layout/AppSidebar.tsx`:**
```typescript
import { IconName } from "lucide-react";

const items = [
  { 
    title: "Feature Name", 
    url: "/features", 
    icon: IconName, 
    roles: [] // or ["admin", "rider"]
  },
];
```

## Type Safety

### Always define interfaces
```typescript
// Good
interface CreateFeatureRequest {
  name: string;
  value: number;
}

// Bad
const createFeature = (data: any) => { ... }
```

### Use enums from backend
```typescript
export enum Status {
  ACTIVE = 'ACTIVE',
  INACTIVE = 'INACTIVE'
}
```

## Error Handling

### API Errors
```typescript
try {
  const result = await featureApi.create(data);
  toast.success("Created successfully");
  return result;
} catch (error) {
  const message = error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'Failed to create';
  toast.error(message);
  throw error;
}
```

### Redux Error State
```typescript
// Always clear errors when retrying
dispatch(clearError());
dispatch(fetchItems());
```

## Code Style

### Import Order
1. React imports
2. Third-party libraries
3. Shadcn/ui components
4. Local imports (hooks, utils, types)

### Component Order
1. Interfaces/Types
2. Component definition
3. Hooks
4. Event handlers
5. Conditional renders
6. Main JSX return

## Performance

### Memoization
- Use `useMemo` for expensive calculations
- Use `useCallback` for event handlers passed to children
- Avoid unnecessary re-renders with `React.memo`

### Code Splitting
- Use lazy loading for route components
- Keep bundle sizes small

## Accessibility

### Always include:
- ARIA labels for interactive elements
- Keyboard navigation support
- Focus management in modals
- Screen reader text where needed

## Backend Integration

### API Base URL
- Dev: `http://localhost:3000`
- JWT tokens in Authorization header
- Handle 401 (redirect to login)
- Handle 403 (show error)

### WebSocket (for tracking)
```typescript
import { io } from 'socket.io-client';

const socket = io('http://localhost:3000/tracking', {
  auth: {
    token: getAuthToken(),
  }
});
```

## Git Workflow

### Commit Messages
```
feat(trips): add trip list page with filters
fix(auth): resolve token refresh issue
test(wallet): add wallet slice tests
docs: update README with setup instructions
```

### Branch Naming
- `feature/trip-list`
- `fix/auth-token`
- `test/reservation-flow`

## Common Pitfalls to Avoid

❌ Don't use card layouts for lists
❌ Don't create full-page forms
❌ Don't use large fonts (stick to text-xs)
❌ Don't skip tests
❌ Don't forget to register Redux slices
❌ Don't forget to add routes and sidebar links
❌ Don't use colors outside the gray palette for text/borders

✅ Do use tables for all lists
✅ Do use modals for forms and details
✅ Do use compact spacing
✅ Do write comprehensive tests
✅ Do follow the auth module structure
✅ Do use TypeScript strictly
✅ Do handle loading and error states

